WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.721
Counting connects one number word to one object

00:00:03.721 --> 00:00:07.042
Touch each dot once as the count grows

00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:14.100
The last number names the whole collection, so stopping at five means that five objects are present.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.825
Separate those same five dots into two groups

00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:23.962
Nothing has entered or left the collection, so its total stays five

00:00:23.962 --> 00:00:29.100
Arrangement changes where objects are; counting measures how many objects there are.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.541
Now add two new dots

00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:37.678
We already know that five are present, so count on: six, seven

00:00:37.678 --> 00:00:44.100
Each new object receives one new number, and the final count records the new total.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.662
Remove the two newly added objects and the count returns to five

00:00:50.662 --> 00:00:53.294
This connection prepares addition and subtraction

00:00:53.294 --> 00:00:59.433
An empty group has count zero, and moving objects alone never creates extra objects.
